UID:75820bed416d7221@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261006T223932Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261006
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] New MaineCare Partner Portal: Multi-Factor Au
 thentication (MFA) Requirements
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			New MaineCare Partner Portal: Multi-Factor Authenticati
 on (MFA) Requirements\nNew MaineCare Partner Portal: Multi-Factor Authenti
 cation (MFA) Requirements\nOct 06\, 2026\nAs a reminder\, the new MaineCar
 e Partner Portal is scheduled to go live on\nOctober 12\, 2026\, at 8:00 A
 M\n. The new portal will replace the current HealthPAS Online Portal and w
 ill require Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA). Read below for more informa
 tion and steps you will need to take to sign into the MaineCare Partner Po
 rtal\nstarting on October 12\n.\nFor all information about the upcoming ch
 anges to MIHMS\, see the “HealthPAS Online Portal” section of the\nPro
 vider Resources\npage.\nMulti-Factor Authenticator (MFA)\nMFA adds a secon
 d verification step after entering your password. This is an important new
  security measure to protect the sensitive information held in the Portal.
  You will have three options to choose from for your additional authentica
 tion factor\; you must choose one.\nFollow the instructions below for firs
 t-time setup of the option you choose.\nMicrosoft Authenticator\nThe Micro
 soft Authenticator app is the recommended MFA method because it offers the
  highest level of protection over other methods. Download the Microsoft Au
 thenticator app\nnow\non a smartphone or tablet so that you are ready to u
 se it on October 12.\nNo sooner than October 12\, follow these steps to se
 t up MFA via the app:\nTrading Partners with existing (migrated) Portal ac
 counts:\nOpen the Microsoft Authenticator app.\nClick “Sign In” on the
  MaineCare Partner Portal\; you will see a User Details window pop up.\nCl
 ick the QR code scanner in the Microsoft Authenticator app and scan the QR
  code displayed on the Portal’s User Details window.\nTrading Partners w
 ithout existing (new or non-migrated) Portal accounts\nwill set this up as
  part of the registration process.\nText/Call\nText (SMS) or call verifica
 tion \nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/new-mai
 necare-partner-portal-multi-factor-authentication-mfa-requirements-2026-10
 -06
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/new-mainec
 are-partner-portal-multi-factor-authentication-mfa-requirements-2026-10-06
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f93982874561796a@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261006T223918Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261006
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Board of Occupational Safety and Health to Ho
 st Listening Sessions on Proposed Indoor Air Quality Compliance Directive
DESCRIPTION:Skip First Level Navigation\nSkip All Navigation\nMaine.gov\nA
 gencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nMaine Departmen
 t of Labor\nContact Us\n|\nNews\n|\nOnline services\n|\nPublications\n|\nS
 itemap\nHome\nContact Us\nOnline Services\nAbout MDOL\nNews & Events\nForm
 s & Publications\nMDOL Bureaus\nHome\n→\nNews & Events\n→ Board of Occ
 upational Safety and Health to Host Listening Sessions on Proposed Indoor 
 Air Quality Compliance Directive\nServices\nJobs & Training\nUnemployment 
 Insurance\nDisability Services\nWorkplace Safety\nLabor Laws\nLabor Statis
 tics\nWorkforce Development\nBoard of Occupational Safety and Health to Ho
 st Listening Sessions on Proposed Indoor Air Quality Compliance Directive\
 nOctober 6\, 2026\nFor Immediate Release\nMedia Contact: Autumn Mahoney\, 
 Communications Specialist\nmedia.dol@maine.gov\nAUGUSTA - The Board of Occ
 upational Safety and Health (BOSH) and the Maine Department of Labor Burea
 u of Labor Standards (BLS) Workplace Safety and Health Division invite int
 erested parties and the public to participate in listening sessions on a\n
 proposed voluntary compliance directive on indoor air quality\n.\nBOSH reg
 ulates and enforces workplace safety and health rules that apply to public
  employers\, including state and local governmental agencies\, school dist
 ricts and quasi-governmental agencies. BOSH is considering publishing a vo
 luntary compliance directive to help public employers monitor and maintain
  healthy indoor air quality in public workplaces. The proposed compliance 
 directive is based in part on the research and recommendations of the Indo
 or Air Quality Advisory Group in 2025.\nBOSH and BLS will host the followi
 ng listening sessions:\nOct. 13\, 2026\, at 1 p.m. at the SafetyWorks! Tra
 ining Institute\, 45 Commerce Dr.\, Augusta\nNov. 2\, 2026\, at 3 p.m. by 
 Zoom with a focus on public school and education employers\nhttps://maines
 tate.zoom.us/j/82302635655?pwd=b1nVGHTd2yeypvjPXwaJlAkK2YhjkL.1\nNov. 9\, 
 2026\, at 10 a.m. by Zoom\nhttps://mainestate.zoom.us/j/89708408033?pwd=XN
 Ua0qqLPRc\nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=1336377
 6
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13363776
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
