DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine State Archives offers expanded digital 
 access with Open Access
DESCRIPTION:AUGUSTA\, MAINE\n– Secretary of State Shenna Bellows today a
 nnounced the official launch of Open Access\, the Maine State Archives (MS
 A) new online platform for publicly accessible\, digitized and born-digita
 l public records. The platform can be accessed at\nhttps://digitalarchives
 .maine.gov\nor from the Maine State Archives section of the Secretary of S
 tate website.\nOpen Access is the public-facing side of a strategic effort
  to maintain a digital preservation system for records of Maine state gove
 rnment. The system ensures the long-term preservation and accessibility of
  state records that are archival or subject to long-term retention.\n“Fr
 om the beginning\, I have been committed to improving efficiency and moder
 nizing our systems to benefit Mainers and streamline access\,” said\nSec
 retary Bellows\n. “Open Access will provide improved government transpar
 ency in a user-friendly platform that will be continuously expanded as mor
 e and more collections are imaged.”\nOverall\, MSA’s collections span 
 five centuries from the 1639 royal land grant to Sir Ferdinand Gorges to t
 he 2024 papers of the Lewiston Tragedy Commission. One section of the site
  is devoted to Maine history before statehood\, highlighting important rec
 ords such as Revolutionary War land grants and the Rolls and Rosters Book 
 of Orders for the 8th Division of the Maine Militia. The records of Maine
 ’s involvement in the Civil War are extensive. Open Access currently hol
 ds just over 100\,000 imaged records so far.\n“With more than 8 miles of
  documents in the Archives care\, there is a long way to go to digitize th
 em all\, but it’s a great start\,” said Maine State Archivist Christia
 n Cotz. “We’re excited to continue to add records to the platform and 
 provide Mainers from students to researchers with even more to discover ea
 ch time they visit the site.”\n###\nhttps://www.maine.gov/sos/news/maine
 -state-archives-offers-expanded-digital-access-open-access
URL:https://www.maine.gov/sos/news/maine-state-archives-offers-expanded-di
 gital-access-open-access
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
